<description>
Fill every row from the nearest marked horizontal bar, turning bar rows and color-boundary ties into separator rows.

Input structure
- A dominant background fills the grid except for full-width horizontal bars and one vertical marker column.
- Outside the marker column, every row is monochrome: either background or a source bar color.
- Background rows share one marker color in the marker column; source bar rows share the other.

Rule
- Each non-source row takes the color of the nearest source bar, with that row's marker-column pixel set to the source-marker color.
- If a row is exactly midway between nearest bars of different colors, make the whole row the source-marker color.
- Each original source bar row becomes a source-marker row with the marker-column pixel changed to the background-row marker color.

Key insight
- The marked bars are horizontal seeds for a one-dimensional nearest-seed partition over rows; equal-distance rows are separators only when the competing seed colors differ.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "marked horizontal bars and the vertical marker column",
  "transform": "recolor each row by the nearest source bar color; each source bar row becomes a marker separator row, and equal-distance rows between different bar colors become plain separator rows"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 16x16 [observed]
  colors:
    background: 7 [observed]
    bg_marker: 8 [observed] -- pixel value in marker column on background rows
    src_marker: 1 [observed] -- pixel value in marker column on source bar rows
    bar_colors: 2-3 distinct, from palette minus {bg, bg_marker, src_marker}
  marker_column: single column at any position (observed range 3-8)
  source_bars:
    count: 2-4 full-width horizontal bars
    each row is monochrome (bar_color) except marker column (src_marker)
    never on row 0 or last row; gap to each edge >= 1
    gap between consecutive bars: 1-8 rows
    same-color bars are consecutive in top-to-bottom order [observed]
  background_rows: monochrome bg except marker column has bg_marker
  transformation:
    each non-bar row takes nearest bar's color; marker column gets src_marker
    each bar row becomes all src_marker with marker column = bg_marker
    midpoint row between different-color bars (even gap) becomes all src_marker (separator)
    midpoint between same-color bars stays as that bar's color (no separator)

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct (input structure is simple enough)
