0001: spec:
0002:   task_type: move_to_match (translate sprites to align marker pixel with matching border anchor)
0003:   grid:
0004:     size: 10-22 rows x 8-22 cols (aspect roughly rectangular, one side 10-14, other 18-22 [observed])
0005:     bg: most common color (any color 1-8)
0006:   anchor (dst):
0007:     count: 1-3 distinct colors, each a single isolated border pixel
0008:     placement: lies on a border row/col (top/bottom/left/right); not a corner [observed]
0009:     isolation: all 4-neighbors equal bg (no other non-bg touching within Manhattan-1 or diagonal)
0010:     axis_rule: top/bottom edge => sprite slides horizontally (match column); left/right edge => slides vertically (match row)
0011:     duplicate_anchors: a color may appear at 2 opposite-edge anchors (same row/col) [observed, test only]
0012:   sprite (src):
0013:     count: 3-5 multi-color connected components in the interior
0014:     colors_per_sprite: 2 (one body color + one marker color); rarely 3 [observed, 1 case]
0015:     marker: exactly 1 pixel, color = least-frequent color inside sprite, must match one anchor color
0016:     body: 4-13 cells of a single non-bg, non-marker color; irregular shape (hollow rect, plus, L, ring, etc.); bounding box 2x3 to 5x7
0017:     marker_position: adjacent (4-neighbor) to body cells, typically on body perimeter or inside hollow; never isolated from body
0018:     connectivity: 8-connected component; interior of sprite may contain bg cells (hollow)
0019:     placement: fully inside grid; sprites do not touch each other or anchors (gap >=1 bg on all sides)
0020:     symmetry: body often has LR or UD symmetry [observed, ~60%]
0021:   extras:
0022:     distractor_singletons: occasionally isolated interior pixels sharing an anchor color act as extra "mini-sprites" that also slide [observed, test_0 only]
0023:     marker_anchor_match: every sprite's marker color must equal some anchor color; multiple sprites may share the same marker color
0024:   transform:
0025:     per_sprite: translate by (dr, dc) so marker aligns with anchor along the axis dictated by anchor edge
0026:     clipping: out-of-bounds pixels after slide are dropped; bg cells under destination are overwritten; non-bg collisions are NOT overwritten
0027:     originals_cleared: source cells become bg; anchors stay in place
0028:   example_layout: |
0029:     ... ... (scatter sprites in interior; each marker color matches one border anchor)
0030:     .888.....
0031:     .848.....    <- sprite marker=4 matches bottom anchor at col 5
0032:     .........
0033:     ....4....    <- bottom anchor (non-corner border)
0034: 
0035: generation_strategy:
0036:   approach: output-first (build settled/aligned state, then invert by scattering sprites away from anchors)
0037:   steps:
0038:     - Choose grid H in [10,22], W in [8,22]; pick bg in [1..8].
0039:     - Choose 1-3 anchor colors (distinct from bg). For each: place a single isolated non-corner border pixel (top/bottom => horizontal-axis anchor; left/right => vertical-axis anchor). Ensure 8-neighborhood (within grid) is all bg.
0040:     - Decide number of sprites N in [3,5]; assign each a marker color from the anchor color set (multiple sprites may share a color).
0041:     - For each sprite, build body in the OUTPUT position (aligned with anchor):
0042:         * Pick a body color (distinct from bg and marker and other sprites' bodies when possible).
0043:         * Generate an irregular small shape (size 4-13, bbox up to 5x7); shape types: hollow rect/ring, plus, L, T, frame-with-gap. Prefer LR or UD symmetry ~60% of the time.
0044:         * Place marker as 1 pixel 4-adjacent to body (perimeter or inside hollow).
0045:         * Position sprite so marker cell equals (anchor_row, chosen_col) for top/bottom anchors, or (chosen_row, anchor_col) for left/right anchors. The "free" axis coordinate is chosen so the sprite fits (with optional partial clipping OK but keep body mostly inside).
0046:         * Ensure sprite body and marker do not touch (8-neighbor) any anchor, any other sprite, or the border (leave >=1 bg gap except where slide clips allowed).
0047:     - Optional (10-20% of grids): add 1-4 distractor singleton pixels of one anchor color scattered in interior (each isolated 8-neighbor), same color as a left/right anchor (they also slide vertically).
0048:     - Invert: for each sprite (and distractor), pick a scatter displacement along the OPPOSITE axis of its slide (horizontal anchors => move sprite vertically away; vertical anchors => move horizontally away) by some random nonzero offset, keeping sprite inside grid and non-overlapping. Remove original aligned sprite pixels (set to bg), paste at scattered location. This yields the input.
0049:     - Self-check: verify by running solver that solver(input) == output.
